{object, key=mt_envelope, name=Envelope, parent=meat_bedroom
    {x_on_desk
        {message
            output={@

Sitting on your desk is an envelope.
            }
        }
    }

    {x_envelope
        {message
            output={@

You examine the envelope.
There is a USB stick inside it.

**(hint: you can put the usb in the computer: #[#ffff00]plug usb into computer#)**
            }
        }
    }







    {input, syntax=[tplt_syntax]((x_envelope))
        {act, logic=x_envelope, tags=!_type|room }
    }

    {input, syntax=[tplt_syntax]((plug_in_usb))
        {set, logic=[player]((objective)), output= }
        {move, logic=hrbr_port, tags=[player]
            output={@

You plug the USB into the computer.
A program begins to run filling the screen with instructions.

1. Apply the self-surgical port receptacle.
1. Attach the 'Tentacle of Cthulhu' cord.
1. Hit 'Enter'.

You excitedly pull out your box of gathered items for this journey.
The self-surgical port is the scariest part. You put latex gloves on AND lather
them with disinfectant. Then you take the cylindrical port and press it to
the back of your neck and grimace, waiting for the pain.

There is a pinprick, then you are numb. You hear a whirring sound as it
embeds itself into your neck.
You feel a bit of pressure as the connections move up into the base of your
skull.
Then it beeps.

**COMPLETE**

You grab the Tentacle of Cthulhu and plug it into one of the computer's open
USB slots and plug the other end into the port in your neck.

You sit comfortably in your desk chair...

And hit Enter.


---


Everything seems to glitch and your body feels like it's vibrating for a
moment.

Everything goes black for a moment.


Then you find yourself in Shellspace!
In a Port Hub.

            }
        }

        {set, logic=[mt_cd]tags, output=-inventory }
        {move, logic=[limbo], tags=[mt_cd] }
        {set, logic=[mt_cd_player]tags, output=-inventory }
        {move, logic=[limbo], tags=[mt_cd_player] }
    }
}
